THIRD-PARTY NOTICES — read this before redistributing

This project contains NO code, binaries or data files from STMicroelectronics.
It is an independent client that can talk to a locally installed copy of
STM32CubeMX (via its documented command line) or run entirely on a data pack
that *you* generate from your own licensed installation (see docs/STANDALONE.md).

Consequences for redistribution:

1. `mxmcp/` sources (server, engine adapter, standalone engine, code generator,
   MCP protocol) are covered by the MIT license above.
2. The generated data pack (`mxmcp/data/cubemx-db.zip`) and everything under
   `analysis/` and `docs/javap/` are DERIVED FROM STMicroelectronics content
   (MCU database, IP mode/config XML, templates, class metadata). They are build
   artifacts for local interoperability and MUST NOT be committed to a public
   repository nor redistributed. `.gitignore` enforces this; CI fails if such a
   file is ever added.
3. STM32CubeMX itself, the STM32Cube firmware packages, CMSIS-Pack contents and
   the ST trademark remain the property of STMicroelectronics and are governed by
   their own licenses (see the `LICENSE*`/`SLA*` files inside the installation).
4. Reverse engineering here is for interoperability, documentation and testing of
   your own installations. You are responsible for complying with the license
   terms of the software you have installed.
